    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d491">

                <pb facs="0567" n="465" xml:id="pg465"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/4921: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-06-28T20:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 28, 1927—8
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>103. Department’s 101 of June 27, 5 P.M., last paragraph.<anchor n="64"
                        xml:id="d491-f1"/> Colonel Stimson states when he left Nicaragua the plan
                    for the Claims Commission was that the Nicaraguan Congress when it has been
                    constituted and called into session shall authorize the creation of a War Claims
                    Commission consisting of an American Chairman, a Liberal and a Conservative, and
                    that the present Commission which is sitting now shall perform merely the work
                    of collecting the claims and the evidence, tabulating them and turning them over
                    to this other Commission for settlement. Moncada<anchor n="65" xml:id="d491-f2"
                    /> who was informed of this plan evidently still believes it is to be carried
                    out as his representative, Señor Morales, so informed Colonel Stimson on June
                    23. If any change in this program has been made the Department desires to be
                    advised and also that you be absolutely sure to obtain the agreement thereto of
                    Moncada and the Liberals. Cable reply. Urgent.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d491-f1" n="64" xml:id="d491-f1-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg400">p. 400</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d491-f2" n="65" xml:id="d491-f2-content">
                <p>Gen. José Maria Moncada, formerly Minister of War and Marine in the Sacasa regime
                    at Puerto Cabezas and commander of the Liberal forces.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
